 "summary": "Fixed semver.coerce truncating prerelease identifiers that begin with a digit (e.g. '2.3.1-nightly.7f3c' -> '2.3.1-nightly.7'). In internal/re.js the PRERELEASEIDENTIFIER token tried the numeric alternative (0|[1-9]\\\\d*) before the non-numeric one, so in the unanchored COERCEFULL/COERCERTLFULL regexes the numeric alternative consumed only the leading digits of an identifier like '7f3c' and the terminus class matched the following letter, so the regex never backtracked to the non-numeric alternative that would match the whole identifier. Swapped the two alternatives (non-numeric first) and updated the comment; anchored regexes such as FULL/LOOSE backtrack to identical results, so parsing/validating behavior is unchanged while coerce with includePrerelease now keeps the full identifier."
}
